From 2a5a6f83f92e7cef3bea61112f66179f644c4f73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:53:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: exact whole-number shader arithmetic (the texture
 cache's 6-texel shift), native 3D draws split only where faces overlap,
 programs kept on the card

The texture cache's shift, found by t14's self-test. Slots in the atlas's first column read
nothing, and every other slot read 6 texels to the left, in both atlas shapes. That is not a
memory or address effect: the vertex shader's slot number came out a hair under the whole number.
bits() was mod(floor(v / exp2(lo)), exp2(n)), and the Vita GPU's exp2(7.0) is a hair over 128, so
slot 127 decoded as 126.98. Its atlas column (mod 16, times 256) then came out 6 texels short, slot
0 wrapped to 127.98 (another place), and bit 15 of 0x8000 read 0 (slot 0 not cached at all).
bits(), the slot's column and row, and every mod and division of whole numbers in the draw and
copy shaders (pmod, the texture window, VRAM wrap, 4/8-bit texel and colour decoding) now round
at each step. The emulated lookup had the same exposure wherever a field's lower bits were all 0
(a page at x 0, a CLUT at x 0).

Native 3D layers (THPS_RENDER3D unset: native, the default; psx stays a fallback). A layer's faces
went to the GPU in a new draw whenever an opaque face already in the draw could be in front of
the next face anywhere on screen: 300-600 draws a frame in a level, each costly in vitaGL. That
test is now per 16x16 cell of a screen grid over the faces' projected bounds, so a draw only
splits where faces overlap. The layer's last draw skips its depth-only pass, since nothing after
it in the layer tests depth. The texture store's per-draw scan is skipped when no cell changed.
The [gl] line gives GL draws a frame, 3D draws a frame, and why 3D draws split (depth, class,
texture, 2D between, layer end).

Start: vitaGL compiles GLSL at every start (shaders ready ~15 s in). A linked program is saved
with glGetProgramBinary to PC_VITA_DIR/shaders/<hash of its sources and the build>.bin and loaded
with glProgramBinary next time. It is used only if every uniform and attribute its sources name
comes out where the compiled program had it, else it is compiled again. THPS_GL_SHADERCACHE=0
always compiles. If the self-test's store row isn't exact, the loaded programs are removed. A
[boot] line gives the time since the start, the programs' time (from the card / compiled) and
the self-test's time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
